<p>The 2026 “<a href="https://www.topuniversities.com/world-university-rankings" target="_blank" rel="noopener">QS World University Rankings</a>” have been published. These contain rankings by subject matter, including philosophy.<span id="more-57007"></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img decoding="async" class="wp-image-57008 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/phi-chart.png" alt="" width="797" height="500" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/phi-chart.png 2366w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/phi-chart-300x188.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/phi-chart-1024x642.png 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/phi-chart-768x482.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/phi-chart-1536x963.png 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/phi-chart-2048x1285.png 2048w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/phi-chart-400x251.png 400w" sizes="(max-width: 797px) 100vw, 797px" /></p>
<p>The rankings are conducted by the London-based education data firm <a href="https://www.qs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quacquarelli Symonds</a>.</p>
<p>As I noted in a post about an earlier version of these rankings:</p>
<div data-google-query-id="CKXgl8TIy5MDFSEKTwgdxiA4Eg">
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>In the QS rankings, a school’s overall score for a particular subject is determined by a <a href="https://support.qs.com/hc/en-gb/articles/4410488025106-QS-World-University-Rankings-by-Subject" target="_blank" rel="noopener">weighted formula</a> that varies by area. In the arts and humanities, for the 2023 results, the formula used is: 60% <a href="https://support.qs.com/hc/en-gb/articles/4405952675346" target="_blank" rel="noopener">academic reputation</a>, 20% <a href="https://support.qs.com/hc/en-gb/articles/4407794203410" target="_blank" rel="noopener">employer reputation</a>, 7.5% <a href="https://support.qs.com/hc/en-gb/articles/4411823915026" target="_blank" rel="noopener">citations per paper</a>, 7.5% <a href="https://support.qs.com/hc/en-gb/articles/360021865539" target="_blank" rel="noopener">H-index</a>, and 5% “<a href="https://support.qs.com/hc/en-gb/articles/360021865579" target="_blank" rel="noopener">International Research Metric</a>“. (It is not clear why these factors are given these particular weights.)</em></p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>QS does not specify whether its rankings are intended to assist prospective undergraduate or graduate students. The rankings have come under fire at various points for <a href="https://www.insidehighered.com/news/2013/05/29/methodology-qs-rankings-comes-under-scrutiny" target="_blank" rel="noopener">methodological concerns</a> as well as <a href="https://www.insidehighered.com/admissions/article/2021/04/27/study-charges-qs-conflicts-interest-international-rankings" target="_blank" rel="noopener">conflicts of interest</a>. Some of the results in philosophy will strike many readers as odd. So be aware that these rankings are controversial (as, of course, is the very idea of fine-grained rankings of places to study philosophy), and take note of alternative sources of information, such as departmental websites, <a href="https://philosophydata.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Academic Philosophy Data &amp; Analysis</a> and the <a href="https://www.philosophicalgourmet.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Philosophical Gourmet Report</a> (noting <a href="https://dailynous.com/2014/10/28/what-do-pgr-evaluators-need-to-know/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">that</a> <a href="https://dailynous.com/2014/10/03/the-pgrs-technical-problems/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">various</a> <a href="https://proteviblog.typepad.com/protevi/2014/10/three-critiques-of-the-pgr.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">criticisms</a> <a href="https://dailynous.com/2021/10/12/enough-ranking-guest-post/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">have</a> <a href="https://dailynous.com/2014/10/08/broader-effects-of-the-pgr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">also</a> been made of the latter).</em></p>
<p>With those caveats in mind, here are the top 50 schools in the <a href="https://www.topuniversities.com/university-subject-rankings/philosophy?items_per_page=100&amp;tab=indicators&amp;sort_by=rank&amp;order_by=asc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2026 QS Rankings in Philosophy</a>:</p>
